# Line endings. Everything in this repository is consumed by Linux — the
# containers, CI, and the production box — so the working tree is LF
# everywhere, on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference. Git on Windows defaults to
# `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. Four shell
# scripts under deploy/backup/ are bind-mounted straight into Linux
# containers (`db-backup` mounts backup.sh), and a CRLF shebang line there
# does not produce a readable error — it produces:
#
#     /backup.sh: line 2: $'\r': command not found
#     /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# on the first nightly backup, i.e. at 01:30, unattended, on the one job
# whose whole purpose is running unattended. The same applies to the
# Dockerfiles, the compose files, and the Caddyfile: all are read by Linux
# tooling that treats a trailing \r as part of the value.
#
# The index is already pure LF (this repo was authored on Linux), so
# adding this changes no file content — it only guarantees a Windows
# checkout matches. If a CRLF file ever does sneak in, fix it with:
#
#     git add --renormalize .
#
# See docs/11-production-deployment.md for the deployment these files feed.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files where CRLF is actively breaking rather
# than merely untidy — spelled out so the reason survives someone
# relaxing the blanket rule above.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
Caddyfile*      text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

# Binary, so git never tries to translate anything inside them.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.dump   binary

# Generated, and reviewed as artifacts rather than read line by line.
# Collapsing them keeps a dependency bump's diff legible.
frontend/package-lock.json  linguist-generated=true
backend/openapi.json        linguist-generated=true
frontend/lib/api/types.ts   linguist-generated=true
